Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||03-11-2000||11:01 AM||||i was out last night with my girlfriend, and i noticed a van following FAR too closelyso i kinda jumped away then slowed down... well, we were sitting at a light and i blipped my throttle (we were in the little cave of a freeway overpass going above us, and i love to hear my exhaust echoing back at me) and i hear this vacuum cleaner "whoooooooooom whoooooooooom" and its the van! not some astro or something, but a full size van! well, i ignore it because streetracing in my area is bad (high police density (not from donuts)) but the light turns green and he pulls from the left lane to the bike lane and passes me on the right and i decide to give him a whuppin. well, now hes on my right, and i roll down the window just to hear him and it sounds pretty quiet, like stock, so i guess it wont be much fun. well, the light turns green, and that van pulls harder than ANY van i have ever seen, and a high pitched whine comes from the van it stays with me through first but i back off halfway through second at about 40 with about a carlength. i think to myself "holy schitt, was that a supercharger?" now i don't have a slow car, i give camaros/poontangh 5.slows a lot of trouble, but that van hauled! definately not a high speed runner, but quick off the line for a VAN! anyone have any experience with really convincing sleepers? the coolest one i know of is a project by my dad and i.. a v-8 1967 vw bug||||reg||1
Z||000001||wkayl||03-11-2000||11:42 AM||||In '74 I had a '67 Mustang coupe with a stock factory 390 high performance. It even had stock hub caps.  The other kids with their sooped up Duster 318's realy got big eyes when i lit em up and left them with their toungs hanging out.  A couple of years ago I was at a car show in Sisteon S Dak (I grew up near Aberdeen S Dak)and there sat my old Mustang in the show.||||reg||1
