Z||000004||batboy||03-11-2000||10:58 PM||||When I was a teen years ago, my Dad took a hotrodded 327 out of an early Camaro and stuck it into a old beat up late 60's van that had a manual three on the tree and 12 bolt 4.11 posi rear end. That old van could scream. My brother and I would take it out and blow people away. It could spin both of those big ol' snow tires in first gear all the way the second, then spin the tires halfway to third, then get a great scratch even in third gear. We got pulled over by a cop once after a smokey burnout showing off to high school buddies. The officer just shook his head and said, if I hadn't seen it, I wouldn't of believed it. I told him the throttle stuck. He just shook his head and said, I'll let you off this time... but you better get that throttle fixed... UNDERSTAND! ***gulp*** Yes sir.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||03-12-2000||12:14 AM||||91 Mitsubishi Mirage 2door hatchback.  CMN built it here for a customer. 3" exhaust Jap spec Aluminum/ceramic turbo running max boost at 22psi ("ONLY 17 around town.." uuuum ok)and the AWD setup from a 90 Eagle Talon. Runs mid 12s in the 1/4 and can smoke all 4 of its widend 14" stock wheels! (215-60)Thats a cool site!  Ever seen 4 smoking piles of rubber not just 2! its Red and has no other obvious marks other then a small sticker that says  CNM on the rear window (bout the size of Credit Card) and bumber sticker that says, "Don't waste my time" I've never ridden in the car but it's at the shop a lot getting more and more go fast goodies added to her..  what a sweet car.  to get a hold of the builder   <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  or TurboCNM@aol.com<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||03-13-2000||09:44 AM||||If if was a full size van, like maybe a 15 passenger van, I can tell you that those things are built to move alot of weight i.e. they have plenty of torque to spare if they arent loaded down with tourists or a sunday school class. It might not growl especially loud because it might have had one 3 inch exhaust pipe on the side opposite you.<P>Just a thought...I used to drive for Budget Rent-a-car when I was in college and I loved to get into a Ford Econoline-250 with that MPFI 351.  It would easily make the tires scream....||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ferrari355||03-13-2000||11:40 AM|||| We had a close race in our 94 intrepid es 3.5ltr with a Neon Sedan. It was really fun becasue we were turning and the neon was behind us and then once we got on the 4 lane road he bascily nailed it and came pretty close to bumping into us so once he got about even with us we were doing about 25 and accelerating he nailed it so mom gave the intrepid alittle gas and we were tie until we got to abotu 60 in a 40 and then we had to turn a Carls JR cause i was hungry but i wanted to continue racing, it was so fun. I'm not sure if i can give this info out but it was an oklahoma tag perljam dark green neon, last bodie style. So if your in oklahoma and see it, it will probably try to race. It was fun though!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000008||Ferrari355||03-13-2000||11:45 AM||||Another embarassing moment for my dad and not me was once he was driving down the road and he was going to pass an Oldsmobile sedan an older like 80's one and it tried to race him well so he floored it and so did the car and it was about 2 car legnths away from my dad and he was so shocked but our TA has a 305 and so now he is planning on building a 350 soon with his own recipe ...HEHEHE.... his last recipe when he had a nova was around 400 HP... Well i better go, TTYL ..bye<BR>Ferrari355||||reg||4
